  "body": "## Why\n\nC225 requires independent finite observations of the fixed candidate's scalar normal-Break result flowing through an outer binding, ordinary Copy and a pure usize predicate actual. A successful process exit alone does not observe that value chain.\n\n## Changes and boundary\n\n- Preserve all V1 and V2 pre-execution source/oracle bytes from Issue #1144. V1 remains NOT_RUN. V2 is explicitly a post-freeze interface-calibrated cohort authorized in comment 6622697245; it is not fresh blind input.\n- Add six positive and six CHECK-only negative inputs, a source-issued owned probe, and a passive observer that preserves every emitted guest C line. Run the unchanged generated guest separately, then compare observed phase/Continue/Break/outer/Copy/actual/selected traces with the frozen oracle at O0/O2.\n- Register one R CTest and a ctest-N-only inventory target. Two existing freeze test registrations use an R-owned copied-snapshot adapter; original validators, manifests, fixtures, Production, workflows and toolchain bytes remain unchanged.\n- Retain raw command/status/output/C/trace evidence in each natural job's R1144_EVIDENCE log envelope. Unexpected semantics stop affected execution and preserve FIRST_RED / later NOT_RUN.\n\n## Independence and apparatus receipts\n\n**pre-execution frozen independent cohort / post-freeze interface-calibrated V2 / incidental old-P formatter exposure after freeze**\n\nC accepted limited continuation in https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1144#issuecomment-6622971928. The unrelated ignored old-P formatter suggestion was never applied. V1 remains NOT_RUN; neither all-period BLIND nor V1 native success is claimed.\n\nBefore semantic execution, R apparatus was corrected to check binding-unit plus typed receiver/initializer/result, classify N6 precision refusal only by the published precision status and codes, and create evidence files exclusively in a fresh output directory. Frozen sources/oracles and Production are unchanged. Initial apparatus HEAD and all FAST failures remain preserved.\n\n## Fixed target\n\nBase: p-c223-loop-result-consumer at 773643d2709a5e5db24650069d67c0d9032fefb0, tree 3d230802ca275bd963101c9b575f1567927f5c7a. Main: acdbf91944a3bac99671d71c6ae23134b56d6c32. Canonical: Draft17.34.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- V1 freeze: https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1144#issuecomment-6622634318\n- V2 approval: https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1144#issuecomment-6622697245\n- V2 freeze: https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1144#issuecomment-6622708609\n- Initial completed-commit-before-ref handoff: https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1144#issuecomment-6622902767\n\nCurrent R HEAD: a835122ead5285cb4496d216814180e58fde48b0, tree a4d4cfdbd56e5093b33bee9017b5b3dcdfb0b2e2.\n\nSame-HEAD FAST verification: https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/actions/runs/41776609675/job/126398330845 — success, attempt 1, exact push checkout, clang-format 23.1.3, GNU 13.3.0 frontend-only build, and one current R registration among 672 unique CTest names (inventory SHA256 938b79cefcf48d8c8bffbb8fb5c1d606182e5d76c5868c7cfd5dfccdecc01770).\n\nFAST actual ledger: 41775881087 failure (FIRST formatter-only; semantic NOT_RUN), 41776114561 success, 41776347672 failure (formatter-only; semantic NOT_RUN), 41776609675 success. FAST is preparation only. Natural ordinary FULL5 + NO-LLVM PARTIAL evidence is pending. Budget is FAST <=6 actual runs, ordinary <=12 actual jobs (initial group plus at most one mechanical repair group), manual0. No local compiler/native/formatter/build/test execution was used.\n\nDRAFT / NEVERMERGE. Finite observations do not prove general soundness. Audit locality UNMEASURED; GO624 PAUSED; H1 HOLD; P1036-PR1050 STOP.",
